<title>INDIA: India's M3 money supply growth rises to 16.15 pct.</title>
<headline>India's M3 money supply growth rises to 16.15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth rose to 16.15 percent on August 26, 1996, from 15.65 percent a fortnight ago, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>	Aug 16, 1996	 Aug 4, 1996     Aug 18, 1995</p>
<p>	    16.15		15.65	     17.23</p>
<p>Broad money supply was 6,303.12 on August 16, 1996 against 6,270.75 billion rupees a fortnight ago and compared to 5,426.80 billion rupees on August 18, 1995, RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
